### Стаття 46

Release from criminal liability in connection with reconciliation of the guilty person with the victim
A person who has committed a criminal misdemeanor or a negligent minor crime for the first time, except for corruption criminal offenses, criminal offenses related to corruption, violations of road safety rules or operation of transport by persons who operated vehicles while intoxicated by alcohol, drugs or other intoxication or were under the influence of medicines that reduce attention and reaction speed, shall be released from criminal liability if such person has reconciled with the victim and compensated for the damage caused or eliminated the harm inflicted.
{Article 46 as amended according to Laws No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1231-IX of 16.02.2021, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021}

### Стаття 47

Release from criminal liability in connection with transfer of a person on surety
1. A person who has committed a criminal misdemeanor or a minor crime for the first time, except for corruption criminal offenses, criminal offenses related to corruption, violations of road safety rules or operation of transport by persons who operated vehicles while intoxicated by alcohol, drugs or other intoxication or were under the influence of medicines that reduce attention and reaction speed, and has sincerely repented, may be released from criminal liability with transfer of such person on surety to a collective of an enterprise, institution or organization at their request, provided that within one year from the date of transfer on surety such person justifies the trust of the collective, does not evade educational measures and does not violate public order.
2. In case of violation of the conditions of transfer on surety, the person shall be brought to criminal liability for the criminal offense committed by such person.
{Article 47 as amended according to Laws No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1231-IX of 16.02.2021, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021}

### Стаття 48

Release from criminal liability in connection with change of circumstances
A person who has committed a criminal misdemeanor or a minor crime for the first time, except for corruption criminal offenses, criminal offenses related to corruption, violations of road safety rules or operation of transport by persons who operated vehicles while intoxicated by alcohol, drugs or other intoxication or were under the influence of medicines that reduce attention and reaction speed, may be released from criminal liability if it is recognized that at the time of criminal proceedings, as a result of a change of circumstances, the act committed by such person has lost its public danger or this person has ceased to be publicly dangerous.
{Article 48 as amended according to Laws No. 4652-VI of 13.04.2012, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1231-IX of 16.02.2021, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021}

### Стаття 49

Release from criminal liability in connection with expiration of limitation periods
1. A person shall be released from criminal liability if the following periods have elapsed from the day of commission of a criminal offense by such person until the day the judgment enters into legal force:
1) two years - in case of commission of a criminal misdemeanor for which a punishment less severe than restriction of liberty is prescribed;
2) three years - in case of commission of a criminal misdemeanor for which punishment in the form of restriction of liberty is prescribed, or in case of commission of a minor crime for which punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a term not exceeding two years is prescribed;
3) five years - in case of commission of a minor crime, except for the case provided for in point 2 of this part;
4) ten years - in case of commission of a grave crime;
5) fifteen years - in case of commission of a particularly grave crime.
2. The running of the limitation period shall be suspended if a person who has committed a criminal offense has evaded pre-trial investigation or court. In these cases, the running of the limitation period shall resume from the day of appearance of the person with confession or detention of such person, and from the time of commission of a criminal misdemeanor - five years. In this case, the person shall be released from criminal liability if fifteen years have elapsed since the commission of the criminal offense.
3. The running of the limitation period shall be interrupted if, before the expiration of the periods specified in parts one and two of this article, the person has committed a new crime, except for a minor crime for which punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a term not exceeding two years is prescribed.
4. The issue of application of the limitation period to a person who has committed a particularly grave crime for which, according to the law, life imprisonment may be imposed, shall be decided by the court. If the court does not consider it possible to apply the limitation period, life imprisonment may not be imposed and shall be replaced by deprivation of liberty for a definite term.
5. The limitation period shall not apply in case of commission of crimes against the foundations of national security of Ukraine provided for in Articles 109-114-2, torture provided for in part three of Article 127, against peace and security of mankind provided for in Articles 437-439 and part one of Article 442 of this Code.
6. In case of commission of a criminal offense provided for in Articles 151-2-156-1, 301-1-303 of this Code against a minor or juvenile person, the calculation of the periods defined in parts one and two of this article shall begin from the day when such victim reached the age of majority or, in case of death of such person, would have reached the age of majority.
{Article 49 as amended according to Laws No. 245-VII of 16.05.2013, No. 1183-VII of 08.04.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1256-IX of 18.02.2021, No. 2160-IX of 24.03.2022, No. 2812-IX of 01.12.2022}

## Розділ X

PUNISHMENT AND ITS TYPES

### Стаття 50. Concept of punishment and its purpose

1. Punishment is a measure of coercion applied on behalf of the state by a court judgment to a person found guilty of committing a criminal offense, and consists in the restriction of rights and freedoms of the convicted person as prescribed by law.
2. Punishment has the purpose not only of penalty, but also of correction of convicted persons, as well as prevention of commission of new criminal offenses both by convicted persons and by other persons.
3. Punishment does not have the purpose of inflicting physical suffering or humiliating human dignity.
{Article 50 as amended according to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
To persons found guilty of committing a criminal offense, the court may apply the following types of punishments:
2) deprivation of military, special rank, grade, title or qualification class;
3) deprivation of the right to hold certain positions or engage in certain activities;
6) service restrictions for military servicemen;
10) detention in a disciplinary battalion of military servicemen;
11) deprivation of liberty for a definite term;
{Article 51 as amended according to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

