### Article 67. Circumstances that Aggravate Punishment

1. When imposing punishment, the following are recognized as circumstances that aggravate it:
1) commission of a crime by a person repeatedly and recidivism of crimes;
2) commission of a criminal offense by a group of persons by prior conspiracy (part two or three of Article 28);
3) commission of a criminal offense on the grounds of racial, national, religious hatred or discord or on the grounds of gender;
4) commission of a criminal offense in connection with the victim's performance of official or public duty;
5) grave consequences caused by the crime;
6) commission of a criminal offense against an elderly person, a person with a disability or a person who is in a helpless state, or a person suffering from a mental disorder, including dementia, having mental development defects, as well as commission of a criminal offense against a minor child or in the presence of a child;
6-1) commission of a criminal offense against a spouse or former spouse or another person with whom the guilty person is (was) in family or close relations;
7) commission of a criminal offense against a woman who was knowingly to the guilty person in a state of pregnancy;
8) commission of a criminal offense against a person who is in material, official or other dependence on the guilty person;
9) commission of a criminal offense using a minor or a person suffering from mental illness or dementia;
10) commission of a crime with particular cruelty;
11) commission of a crime using the conditions of martial law or a state of emergency, other emergency events;
12) commission of a crime in a generally dangerous manner;
13) commission of a criminal offense by a person who is in a state of alcoholic intoxication or in a state caused by the use of narcotic or other intoxicating substances.
2. The court has the right, depending on the nature of the criminal offense committed, not to recognize any of the circumstances specified in part one of this Article, with the exception of the circumstances specified in points 2, 6, 6-1, 7, 9, 10, 12 as aggravating punishment, having stated the reasons for its decision in the verdict.
3. When imposing punishment, the court may not recognize as aggravating it circumstances not specified in part one of this Article.
4. If any of the circumstances that aggravate punishment is provided for in an Article of the Special Part of this Code as a feature of a criminal offense that affects its qualification, the court may not take it into account again when imposing punishment as one that aggravates it.
{Article 67 as amended according to Laws No. 2227-VIII of 06.12.2017, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Article 68

Imposition of Punishment for an Uncompleted Criminal Offense and for a Criminal Offense Committed in Complicity
1. When imposing punishment for an uncompleted criminal offense, the court, guided by the provisions of Articles 65-67 of this Code, takes into account the degree of gravity of the act committed by the person, the degree of implementation of the criminally unlawful intent and the reasons due to which the criminal offense was not brought to completion.
2. For the commission of preparation for a crime, the term or amount of punishment may not exceed half of the maximum term or amount of the most severe type of punishment provided for by the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code.
3. For the commission of an attempt at a criminal offense, the term or amount of punishment may not exceed two thirds of the maximum term or amount of the most severe type of punishment provided for by the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code.
4. Life imprisonment for the commission of preparation for a crime and the commission of an attempt at a crime is not applied, except in cases of commission of crimes against the foundations of national security of Ukraine provided for in Articles 110, 111, 111-1, 112, 113, against peace, security of humanity and international legal order provided for in Articles 437-439, part one of Article 442 and Article 443 of this Code.
5. When imposing punishment on accomplices in a criminal offense, the court, guided by the provisions of Articles 65-67 of this Code, takes into account the nature and degree of participation of each of them in the commission of the criminal offense.
{Article 68 as amended according to Laws No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008, No. 1492-VIII of 07.09.2016, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 2160-IX of 24.03.2022, No. 3233-IX of 13.07.2023}

### Article 69. Imposition of a Milder Punishment than Provided for by Law

1. In the presence of several circumstances that mitigate punishment and substantially reduce the degree of gravity of the criminal offense committed, taking into account the personality of the guilty person, the court, having motivated its decision, may, except in cases of conviction for a corruption criminal offense, a criminal offense related to corruption, a criminal offense provided for in Articles 403, 405, 407, 408, 429 of this Code committed under conditions of martial law or in combat situation, for torture committed by a representative of the state, including a foreign one, impose a principal punishment below the lowest limit established in the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code, or move to another, milder type of principal punishment not specified in the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code for this criminal offense. In this case, the court does not have the right to impose a punishment below the lowest limit established for such type of punishment in the General Part of this Code. For the commission of a criminal offense for which a principal punishment in the form of a fine in the amount of more than three thousand non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens is provided, the court on the grounds provided for in this part may impose a principal punishment in the form of a fine, the amount of which is not more than one quarter lower than the lowest limit established in the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code.
2. On the grounds provided for in part one of this Article, the court may not impose an additional punishment that is provided for in the sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code as mandatory, except in cases of imposing punishment for the commission of a criminal offense for which a principal punishment in the form of a fine in the amount of more than three thousand non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens is provided.
{Article 69 as amended according to Laws No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008, No. 4025-VI of 15.11.2011, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021, No. 2812-IX of 01.12.2022, No. 2839-IX of 13.12.2022}

### Article 69

1. Imposition of Punishment in the Presence of Circumstances that Mitigate Punishment
1. In the presence of circumstances that mitigate punishment provided for in points 1 and 2 of part one of Article 66 of this Code, the absence of circumstances that aggravate punishment, and also upon the accused's acknowledgment of his guilt, the term or amount of punishment may not exceed two thirds of the maximum term or amount of the most severe type of punishment provided for by the corresponding sanction of the Article (sanction of part of the Article) of the Special Part of this Code.
{The Code was supplemented with Article 69-1 according to Law No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008; as amended according to Law No. 245-VII of 16.05.2013}

