### Стаття 84

1. Release from serving a sentence in connection with the adoption by an authorized body of a decision to transfer a convicted person for exchange as a prisoner of war
1. A convicted person, with respect to whom during the serving of a sentence in the form of correctional labor, arrest, restriction of liberty, detention in a disciplinary battalion of military servicemen, deprivation of liberty for a definite term, life imprisonment, an authorized body has adopted a decision on his or her transfer for exchange as a prisoner of war and who has provided written consent to conduct such an exchange, shall be released by the court from serving the imposed sentence.
2. If the exchange of such a convicted person did not take place, the court, upon the motion of the prosecutor, shall adopt a decision on sending the convicted person released from serving the sentence in connection with his or her transfer for exchange as a prisoner of war for further serving of the previously imposed sentence.
3. In the event that a person who was released by the court from serving a sentence in connection with the adoption by an authorized body of a decision on his or her transfer for exchange as a prisoner of war and such exchange took place, commits a new criminal offense during the unserved part of the sentence, the court shall impose a sentence on him or her according to the rules provided for by Articles 71 and 72 of this Code.
{The Code was supplemented with Article 84-1 in accordance with Law No. 2472-IX of 28.07.2022; as amended in accordance with Law No. 2810-IX of 01.12.2022}

### Стаття 85

Release from punishment on the basis of the law of Ukraine on amnesty or an act of pardon
On the basis of a law on amnesty or an act of pardon, a convicted person may be fully or partially released from the principal and additional punishments.
{Text of Article 85 as amended by Law No. 3465-VI of 02.06.2011}
1. Amnesty is declared by a law of Ukraine with respect to a certain category of persons.
2. By a law on amnesty, persons found guilty of committing a criminal offense by a conviction of a court, or criminal cases concerning whom have been considered by courts, but the sentences with respect to these persons have not entered into legal force, may be fully or partially released from serving the sentence.
{Part three of Article 86 was excluded on the basis of Law No. 3465-VI of 02.06.2011}
4. Persons found guilty of committing high treason, sabotage, corruption criminal offenses, criminal offenses related to corruption, violation of traffic safety rules or operation of transport by persons who operated vehicles while intoxicated by alcohol, drugs or other intoxication or were under the influence of medicines that reduce attention and speed of reaction, the sentences with respect to whom have not entered into legal force, may not be released from serving the sentence, and persons the sentences with respect to whom have entered into legal force may not be fully released by a law on amnesty from serving the sentence. The specified persons may be released from serving the sentence after actual serving by them of the terms established by part three of Article 81 of this Code.
{Article 86 as amended in accordance with Laws No. 3465-VI of 02.06.2011, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1231-IX of 16.02.2021, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021, No. 2113-IX of 03.03.2022}
1. Pardon is exercised by the President of Ukraine with respect to an individually determined person.
2. By an act of pardon, a replacement may be made for a convicted person of the sentence imposed by the court in the form of life imprisonment with deprivation of liberty for a term of not less than twenty-five years.
3. Persons convicted of committing corruption criminal offenses, criminal offenses related to corruption, violation of traffic safety rules or operation of transport by persons who operated vehicles while intoxicated by alcohol, drugs or other intoxication or were under the influence of medicines that reduce attention and speed of reaction, may be released from serving the sentence by way of pardon after actual serving by them of the terms established by part three of Article 81 of this Code.
{Article 87 as amended in accordance with Laws No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1231-IX of 16.02.2021, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021}

### Стаття 88. Legal consequences of a criminal record

1. A person is recognized as having a criminal record from the day the conviction enters into legal force until the expungement or removal of the criminal record.
2. A criminal record has legal significance in the event of committing a new criminal offense, as well as in other cases provided for by the laws of Ukraine.
3. Persons convicted by a court sentence without imposition of punishment or with release from punishment or those who have served a sentence for an act the criminal unlawfulness and punishability of which has been eliminated by law, are recognized as not having a criminal record.
4. Persons who have been rehabilitated are recognized as not having a criminal record.
{Article 88 as amended in accordance with Laws No. 4025-VI of 15.11.2011, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 89. Terms of expungement of a criminal record

The following are recognized as not having a criminal record:
1) persons convicted in accordance with Article 75 of this Code, if during the probationary period they do not commit a new criminal offense and if during the specified period the decision on release from serving the sentence with probation is not revoked on other grounds provided for by law. If the term of the additional punishment exceeds the duration of the probationary period, the person is recognized as not having a criminal record after serving this additional punishment;
2) women convicted in accordance with Article 79 of this Code, if during the probationary period they do not commit a new criminal offense and if after the expiration of this period a decision is not adopted on sending them to serve the sentence imposed by the court sentence. If the convicted woman was not released from the additional punishment and its term exceeds the duration of the probationary period, then the woman is recognized as not having a criminal record after serving this additional punishment;
2-1) persons convicted of committing a criminal misdemeanor, after serving the sentence;
{Paragraph 3 of Article 89 was excluded on the basis of Law No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014}
4) persons who have served a sentence in the form of service restriction for military servicemen or detention in a disciplinary battalion of military servicemen or were released early from these punishments, as well as military servicemen who have served a sentence in a guardhouse instead of arrest;
5) persons convicted of committing a crime to a principal punishment in the form of a fine in the amount of not more than three thousand non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens, deprivation of the right to occupy certain positions or engage in certain activities, community service, correctional labor or arrest, if they within one year from the day of serving the sentence (principal and additional) do not commit a new criminal offense;
6) persons convicted of committing a crime to restriction of liberty, if they within two years from the day of serving the sentence (principal and additional) do not commit a new criminal offense;
7) persons convicted to deprivation of liberty or a principal punishment in the form of a fine for a minor crime, if they within three years from the day of serving the sentence (principal and additional) do not commit a new criminal offense;
8) persons convicted to deprivation of liberty or a principal punishment in the form of a fine for a grave crime, if they within six years from the day of serving the sentence (principal and additional) do not commit a new criminal offense;
9) persons convicted to deprivation of liberty or a principal punishment in the form of a fine for a particularly grave crime, if they within eight years from the day of serving the sentence (principal and additional) do not commit a new criminal offense.
{Article 89 as amended in accordance with Laws No. 4025-VI of 15.11.2011, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

