### Article 90. Calculation of periods for expungement of conviction

1. Periods for expungement of conviction are calculated from the day of serving the principal and additional punishment.
2. The period for expungement of conviction includes the time during which the sentence was not executed, if the statute of limitations for execution of the sentence was not interrupted. If the sentence was not executed, the conviction is expunged upon expiration of the statute of limitations for execution of the sentence.
3. If a person was released early from serving punishment, the period for expungement of conviction is calculated from the day of early release from serving punishment (principal and additional).
4. If the unserved part of punishment was replaced by a milder punishment, the period for expungement of conviction is calculated from the day of serving the milder punishment (principal and additional).
5. If a person who has served punishment commits a criminal offense again before the expiration of the period for expungement of conviction, the running of the period for expungement of conviction is interrupted and is calculated anew. In these cases, the periods for expungement of conviction are calculated separately for each criminal offense after actual serving of punishment (principal and additional) for the last criminal offense.
{Article 90 as amended pursuant to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
1. If a person after serving punishment in the form of restriction of liberty or deprivation of liberty has proven their correction by exemplary conduct and conscientious attitude to work, the court may remove the conviction from them before the expiration of the periods specified in Article 89 of this Code.
2. Removal of conviction before the expiration of the periods specified in Article 89 of this Code is not permitted in cases of conviction for intentional grave and especially grave, as well as corruption criminal offenses or criminal offenses related to corruption.
3. Removal of conviction is permitted only after the expiration of at least half of the period for expungement of conviction specified in Article 89 of this Code.
4. The procedure for removal of conviction is established by the Criminal Procedure Code of Ukraine.
{Article 91 as amended pursuant to Laws No. 4652-VI of 13.04.2012, No. 1698-VII of 14.10.2014, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018, No. 1576-IX of 29.06.2021}

## Section XIII-1

RESTRICTIVE MEASURES

### Article 91

1. Restrictive measures applied to persons who have committed domestic violence
1. In the interests of a victim of a crime related to domestic violence, simultaneously with imposition of punishment not related to deprivation of liberty, or release on grounds provided for by this Code from criminal liability or punishment, the court may apply to a person who has committed domestic violence one or several restrictive measures, according to which the following obligations may be imposed on the convicted person:
1) prohibition to stay in a place of joint residence with a person who has suffered from domestic violence;
2) restriction of communication with a child in case domestic violence was committed against a child or in their presence;
3) prohibition to approach within a specified distance to a place where a person who has suffered from domestic violence may permanently or temporarily reside, temporarily or systematically be present in connection with work, study, treatment or for other reasons;
4) prohibition of correspondence, telephone conversations with a person who has suffered from domestic violence, other contacts through means of communication or electronic communications personally or through third persons;
5) referral for completion of a program for offenders.
2. Measures provided for by part one of this Article are applied to a person who at the time of committing domestic violence has reached 18 years of age.
3. Measures provided for by part one of this Article may be applied for a period from one to three months and if necessary may be extended for a period determined by the court, but not more than 12 months.
{Part four of Article 91-1 excluded on the basis of Law No. 3233-IX of 13.07.2023}
{Article 91-1 as amended pursuant to Law No. 3233-IX of 13.07.2023}
