### Стаття 97

Release from criminal liability with application of compulsory measures of educational character
1. A minor who has committed a criminal offence or a negligent minor crime for the first time may be released from criminal liability if his or her correction is possible without application of punishment. In these cases, the court shall apply to the minor compulsory measures of educational character provided for in part two of Article 105 of this Code.
2. Compulsory measures of educational character provided for in part two of Article 105 of this Code shall also be applied by the court to a person who, before reaching the age from which criminal liability may arise, has committed a socially dangerous act falling under the characteristics of an act provided for in the Special Part of this Code.
3. In case of evasion by a minor who has committed a criminal offence from application to him or her of compulsory measures of educational character, these measures shall be cancelled and he or she shall be brought to criminal liability.
{Article 97 as amended according to Laws No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
1. The following basic types of punishments may be applied by the court to minors found guilty of committing a criminal offence:
5) deprivation of liberty for a definite term.
2. Additional punishments in the form of a fine and deprivation of the right to hold certain positions or engage in certain activities may be applied to minors.
{Article 98 as amended according to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
1. A fine shall be applied only to minors who have independent income, own funds or property against which recovery may be enforced.
2. The amount of the fine, including for committing a criminal offence for which the basic punishment is provided only in the form of a fine exceeding three thousand non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens, shall be established by the court depending on the gravity of the criminal offence committed and taking into account the property status of the minor within the limits of up to five hundred non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens established by law.
3. To a minor who does not have independent income, own funds or property against which recovery may be enforced, convicted of committing a criminal offence for which the basic punishment is provided only in the form of a fine exceeding three thousand non-taxable minimum incomes of citizens, punishment in the form of community service or correctional labour may be applied in accordance with the provisions of Articles 100, 103 of this Code.
{Article 99 as amended according to Laws No. 4025-VI of 15.11.2011, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 100. Community service and correctional labour

1. Community service may be assigned to a minor aged 16 to 18 years for a term from thirty to one hundred and twenty hours and consists in performance by the minor of work during time free from studies or main work. The duration of performance of this type of punishment may not exceed two hours per day.
2. Correctional labour may be assigned to a minor aged 16 to 18 years at the place of work for a term from two months to one year.
3. From the earnings of a minor sentenced to correctional labour, a deduction to the income of the state shall be made in the amount established by the court judgment, within the limits from five to ten percent.
Arrest consists in keeping a minor who has reached the age of sixteen at the time of pronouncement of the judgment under conditions of isolation in specially adapted institutions for a term from fifteen to forty-five days.

### Стаття 102. Deprivation of liberty for a definite term

1. Punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty to persons who have not reached the age of eighteen before committing a crime may be assigned for a term from six months to ten years, except for cases provided for in point 5 of part three of this Article. Minors sentenced to punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty shall serve it in special educational institutions.
{Part two of Article 102 excluded on the basis of Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
3. Punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty shall be assigned to a minor:
{Point 1 of part three of Article 102 excluded on the basis of Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}
2) for a minor crime - for a term not exceeding four years;
3) for a grave crime - for a term not exceeding seven years;
4) for a particularly grave crime - for a term not exceeding ten years;
5) for a particularly grave crime combined with intentional deprivation of human life - for a term of up to fifteen years.
{Article 102 as amended according to Laws No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008, No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 103. Assignment of punishment

1. When assigning punishment to a minor, the court, in addition to the circumstances provided for in Articles 65-67 of this Code, shall take into account the conditions of his or her life and upbringing, the influence of adults, the level of development and other characteristics of the personality of the minor.
2. When assigning punishment to a minor for a totality of criminal offences or judgments, the final punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty may not exceed fifteen years.
{Article 103 as amended according to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 104. Release from serving punishment with probation

1. Release from serving punishment with probation shall be applied to minors in accordance with Articles 75-78 of this Code, taking into account the provisions provided for in this Article.
2. Release from serving punishment with probation may be applied to a minor only in case of his or her sentencing to arrest or deprivation of liberty.
3. The probation period shall be established for a duration from one to two years.
4. In case of release of a minor from serving punishment with probation, the court may impose on a separate person, with his or her consent or at his or her request, the obligation to supervise the convicted person and conduct educational work with him or her.
{Article 104 as amended according to Law No. 270-VI of 15.04.2008}

### Стаття 105

Release from punishment with application of compulsory measures of educational character
1. A minor who has committed a criminal offence or a minor crime may be released by the court from punishment if it is found that as a result of sincere repentance and subsequent impeccable behaviour he or she does not require application of punishment at the time of pronouncement of the judgment.
2. In this case, the court shall apply to the minor the following compulsory measures of educational character:
2) restriction of leisure and establishment of special requirements for the behaviour of the minor;
3) transfer of the minor under the supervision of parents or persons replacing them, or under the supervision of a pedagogical or labour collective with its consent, as well as separate citizens at their request;
4) imposition on a minor who has reached the age of fifteen and has property, funds or earnings, of the obligation to compensate for property damage caused;
5) referral of the minor to a special educational institution for children and adolescents until his or her correction, but for a term not exceeding three years. The conditions of stay in these institutions of minors and the procedure for their leaving shall be determined by law.
3. Several compulsory measures of educational character provided for in part two of this Article may be applied to a minor. The duration of measures of educational character provided for in points 2 and 3 of part two of this Article shall be established by the court that assigns them.
4. The court may also recognize it necessary to appoint an educator for the minor in the procedure provided for by law.
{Article 105 as amended according to Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

