### Стаття 106

Release from criminal liability and serving of punishment in connection with expiration of limitation periods
1. Release from criminal liability and serving of punishment in connection with expiration of limitation periods for persons who committed a criminal offense before reaching the age of eighteen is applied in accordance with Articles 49 and 80 of this Code, taking into account the provisions stipulated by this Article.
2. For persons specified in part one of this Article, the following limitation periods are established:
1) two years - in case of committing a criminal misdemeanor;
2) five years - in case of committing a minor crime;
3) seven years - in case of committing a grave crime;
4) ten years - in case of committing a particularly grave crime.
3. For persons specified in part one of this Article, the following periods for execution of a conviction sentence are established:
1) two years - in case of sentencing to a punishment not related to deprivation of liberty, as well as when sentencing to punishment for a criminal misdemeanor;
2) five years - in case of sentencing to punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a minor crime, as well as when sentencing to punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a term not exceeding five years for a grave crime;
3) seven years - in case of sentencing to punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a term exceeding five years for a grave crime;
4) ten years - in case of sentencing to punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a particularly grave crime.
{Article 106 as amended in accordance with Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 107. Conditional early release from serving of punishment

1. Conditional early release from serving of punishment may be applied to persons serving punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a criminal offense committed before reaching the age of eighteen, regardless of the gravity of the committed criminal offense.
2. Conditional early release from serving of punishment may be applied if the convicted person has proven their correction through conscientious behavior and attitude to work and study.
3. Conditional early release from serving of punishment may be applied to persons convicted for a criminal offense committed before reaching the age of eighteen, after actual serving of:
1) not less than one third of the assigned term of punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a minor crime and for a negligent grave crime;
2) not less than half of the term of punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty assigned by the court for an intentional grave crime or a negligent particularly grave crime, as well as if the person previously served punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for an intentional criminal offense and before expungement or removal of conviction committed again before reaching the age of eighteen a new intentional criminal offense for which they were sentenced to deprivation of liberty;
3) not less than two thirds of the term of punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty assigned by the court for an intentional particularly grave crime, as well as if the person previously served punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty and was conditionally released early from serving of punishment, but before the end of the unserved part of punishment and before reaching the age of eighteen committed again an intentional criminal offense for which they were sentenced to deprivation of liberty.
4. Replacement of the unserved part of punishment with a milder punishment is not applied to minors.
5. In case a person to whom conditional early release from serving of punishment was applied commits a new criminal offense during the unserved part of punishment, the court assigns them punishment according to the rules stipulated in Articles 71 and 72 of this Code.
{Article 107 as amended in accordance with Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

### Стаття 108. Expungement and removal of conviction

1. Expungement and removal of conviction for persons who committed a criminal offense before reaching the age of eighteen is carried out in accordance with Articles 88-91 of this Code, taking into account the provisions stipulated by this Article.
2. The following minors are recognized as having no conviction:
1) sentenced to punishment not related to deprivation of liberty, after execution of this punishment;
2) sentenced to deprivation of liberty for a minor crime, if they do not commit a new criminal offense within one year from the day of serving the punishment;
3) sentenced to deprivation of liberty for a grave crime, if they do not commit a new criminal offense within three years from the day of serving the punishment;
4) sentenced to deprivation of liberty for a particularly grave crime, if they do not commit a new criminal offense within five years from the day of serving the punishment.
3. Early removal of conviction is permitted only for a person who served punishment in the form of deprivation of liberty for a grave or particularly grave crime committed before reaching the age of eighteen, on the grounds stipulated in part one of Article 91 of this Code, after expiration of not less than half of the term of expungement of conviction specified in part two of this Article.
{Article 108 as amended in accordance with Law No. 2617-VIII of 22.11.2018}

## Розділ I

CRIMES AGAINST THE FOUNDATIONS OF NATIONAL SECURITY OF UKRAINE

### Стаття 109

Actions aimed at violent change or overthrow of the constitutional order or at seizure of state power
1. Actions committed with the purpose of violent change or overthrow of the constitutional order or seizure of state power, as well as conspiracy to commit such actions, -
are punishable by deprivation of liberty for a term of five to ten years with confiscation of property or without such.
2. Public calls for violent change or overthrow of the constitutional order or for seizure of state power, as well as distribution of materials with calls to commit such actions, -
are punishable by restriction of liberty for a term up to three years or deprivation of liberty for the same term with confiscation of property or without such.
3. Actions stipulated by part two of this Article, committed by a person who is a representative of authority, or repeatedly, or by an organized group, or using mass media, -
are punishable by restriction of liberty for a term up to five years or deprivation of liberty for the same term with confiscation of property or without such.
{Article 109 as amended in accordance with Law No. 721-VII of 16.01.2014 - became invalid on the basis of Law No. 732-VII of 28.01.2014; as amended in accordance with Laws No. 767-VII of 23.02.2014, No. 1689-VII of 07.10.2014}

### Стаття 110. Encroachment on territorial integrity and inviolability of Ukraine

1. Intentional actions committed with the purpose of changing the boundaries of territory or state border of Ukraine in violation of the procedure established by the Constitution of Ukraine, as well as public calls or distribution of materials with calls to commit such actions, -
are punishable by deprivation of liberty for a term of three to five years with confiscation of property or without such.
2. The same actions, if they are committed by a person who is a representative of authority, or repeatedly, or by a group of persons by prior conspiracy, or combined with incitement of national or religious enmity, -
are punishable by deprivation of liberty for a term of five to ten years with confiscation of property or without such.
3. Actions stipulated by parts one or two of this Article, which resulted in death of people or other grave consequences, -
are punishable by deprivation of liberty for a term of ten to fifteen years or life imprisonment with confiscation of property or without such.
{Article 110 as amended in accordance with Laws No. 1183-VII of 08.04.2014, No. 1689-VII of 07.10.2014}

